From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: pinephone: keep USB-C port in peripheral mode

PHY 0 (the USB-C port) is shared between the MUSB OTG controller and the
EHCI0/OHCI0 host controllers. When EHCI0/OHCI0 probe, usb_add_hcd() sets
the PHY to host mode ("phy-1c19400.phy.0: Changing dr_mode to 1"), which
overrides dr_mode = "peripheral" on usb_otg: the PHY routes the port to
the host controllers and MUSB ends up in a_wait_vrise, so the USB gadget
never shows up on the host.

This firmware only uses the port as a peripheral (console, network,
updates), so disable the host controllers on it.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
@@ -161,7 +161,8 @@
 };

 &ehci0 {
-	status = "okay";
+	/* Shares PHY 0 with usb_otg and would force it into host mode */
+	status = "disabled";
 };

 &ehci1 {
@@ -298,7 +299,8 @@
 };

 &ohci0 {
-	status = "okay";
+	/* Shares PHY 0 with usb_otg and would force it into host mode */
+	status = "disabled";
 };

 &ohci1 {
